## 5️⃣ Alignment & Divergence – Where Both Sides Agree

| Area | Optimist Position | Critic Position | Consensus |
|------|-------------------|-----------------|-----------|
| **Market demand exists** | Yes – wellness & home‑comfort trends. | Yes – but saturated & price‑elastic. | Demand is real, but competition is fierce; price must be competitive. |
| **Sustainability matters** | Essential for branding. | Adds cost & scrutiny. | Eco‑claims help, but start with low‑cost, verifiable steps before expensive certifications. |
| **Storytelling is valuable** | Must be central. | Professional storytelling costs money. | Content is needed; begin with low‑budget user‑generated material, upgrade later. |
| **Personalization can command premium** | Yes – custom scents, monograms. | Increases complexity & CAC. | Offer limited‑scope personalization (pre‑set bundles) to balance premium pricing with operational simplicity. |
| **Subscription can stabilize cash flow** | Yes – “Candle of the month.” | High churn & logistics burden. | Test a *mini‑subscription* (e.g., 3‑month trial) before full‑scale rollout. |

